<p>The question now is, how do we find these endpoints?</p>
<p><strong>Obtaining the endpoints of each index=E2=80=99s segment on the l=
ine</strong><br>
A key observation is that the endpoint of a segment is equal to the length =
of all previous segments, plus the length of the current segment. We can se=
e how this works below:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
